In /testbed, look at crates/biome_service/src/embed/html.rs (and the html parser/syntax for Astro). For an Astro file `---
import MyComponent from './my-component.astro';
const text = "abc";
---

<MyComponent {text} />
`, the `{text}` is a shorthand attribute (HtmlSingleTextExpression / HtmlAttributeSingleTextExpression?) on a component. Determine which node kinds get embedded (parsed as JS snippets) and why a single-text-expression attribute `{text}` on an element is not picked up as a reference (note the playground code is `<MyComponent {text} />`). Find the exact code to fix and propose a diff. Also check the existing tests/snapshots for astro in crates/biome_js_analyze/tests/specs/correctness/noUnusedVariables or biome_service.

In /testbed/crates/biome_service/src/file_handlers/html/parse_embedded_nodes.rs, in the HtmlVariant::Astro loop, right after the HtmlSingleTextExpression block, add this block (mirroring the Svelte branch ~lines 340-355 for exact style):
if let Some(attr) = HtmlAttributeSingleTextExpression::cast_ref(&element) && !attr.syntax().parent().is_some_and(|p| HtmlAttributeInitializerClause::can_cast(p.kind())) && let Ok(expression) = attr.expression() && let Some(candidate) = build_text_expression_candidate(&expression) { ctx.parse_and_push(&candidate, &doc_file_source, None, &mut nodes); }
Match whatever the Svelte branch does exactly. Then run `cargo check -p biome_service` and report.

